    skos:definition "the crude ore from which metal is obtained by smelting. In 1855, there was raised in Cornwall 161,375 tons of copper ore; in Devonshire, 34,024; in Ireland, 15,063 tons. In the year ending June 1856, the copper ore raised in Cornwall amounted to 209,305 tons, valued at £1,283,639. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 117]"@en ;
